  "question": {
    "text": "The number of undecayed nuclei N in a sample of radioactive material as a function of time $(\\mathrm{t})$ is shown in the figure. Which of the following graphs correctly show the relationship between $N$ and the activity ' $A$ ' ?\n\n\n<img width=\"250px\" src=\"assets\\qt0002_f86101eedc93.png\"/><br/>"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<img width=\"250px\" src=\"assets\\ot1_0002_96e7fa1df9e2.png\"/><br/>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<img width=\"250px\" src=\"assets\\ot2_0002_a5b400440167.png\"/><br/>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<img width=\"250px\" src=\"assets\\ot3_0002_ede8be0942d9.png\"/><br/>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<img width=\"250px\" src=\"assets\\ot4_0002_78eaaa850d54.png\"/><br/>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\begin{aligned}\n& N=N_0 e^{-\\lambda t} \\\\\n& -\\frac{d N}{d t}=-N_0(-\\lambda) e^{-\\lambda t}\n\\end{aligned}$\n$\\mathrm{A}=+\\mathrm{N} \\lambda$\n\nStraight line passing through origin."
  }
}